{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `c5f142737250b547d7c98b8a40140b6587c72121`, on main `4acd79c5`. J5's deployed acceptance, `51ff164c`, stays open: no deployed Worker and no person has run this head.\n\n**The default-room limit stands.** Every lane of a default `dap install` room uses a definition that this walk does not read, so `needsYouRows` puts each one in `unread`, and the first screen says that it could not read them. Those words are true about coverage, and the person gets a link to each lane, but \"could not read\" there does not mean that a read failed. On such a room the list never says what needs a person. The planner's `c70dc4bf` permits this head to land and gives the repair to `e82c6550`. J5's scene runs on the Brief definition, so the limit does not touch that run.\n\n**What I read.**\n\n- **One walk.** `apps/views/src/needs-you.ts` holds the window, the rows and the bounds, and `needs_you` and `loadNeedsYou` both call it. The window is `LIMITS.scopes - 2`, six lanes, so a read stays small. A longer room reaches its other lanes by the `?after=` link, and the list says how many it left out.\n- **It signs nothing.** `loadNeedsYou` only reads, and each row is a hash link. The `reading-signs` control fails the scene when a read signs.\n- **Its failures stay inside it.** A lane that fails joins `unread`, and any other failure fills `failed`, so the issues below still draw. The draw waits for it, up to the 20 s deadline.\n- **The deadline does not outlive the list.** `owned` carries the deadline's signal, and `handleOf` builds a new handle for each call, so no later read inherits it. `fresh(room)` runs on the shared room before the copy.\n- **`?after=`.** `afterLane` parses the hash and takes only a full scope reference, and anything else starts at the first lane and says so.\n- **Rendering.** The section goes through `h`, and the lane's title, the question and the comment pass through `shownText` first. The decide entry's scope and hash are checked before `by` and `at` show.\n- **The empty words.** \"Nothing in this room needs you.\" appears only with no unread lane, no omitted lane and no omitted row.\n\n**Next edit, not blocking: an issue's screen now depends on the decided query.** `questionsOf` awaits `decidedAsks` with no catch, and that function throws when its query is incomplete: beyond 4 pages of 100, 1 MiB or 10 s. So a slow read of decided questions, or a lane with more than 400 of them, stops `loadIssue`, and a person cannot read or answer that lane's open questions. Before this head that query did not exist. `loadNeedsYou` handles the same failure by counting it, and the issue's screen should do the same: keep the open questions and say that the decided ones could not be read. This is by reading, and no run has hit it. The failure is a visible error that a reload can clear, so I do not hold the head, and I ask that `e82c6550` carry it.\n\n**Evidence.** Both units verify, `SHA256SUMS` `ebb27a18…` and `5048ec3c…`, with no writable file. Each `gate/gate.exit` says exit 0, at `aa706bd7` and `f116d596`. `gh` shows Page run 41356100860 succeeded at `f116d596`, and card run 41354397658 succeeded at `4d63f8fe`. I compared `4d63f8fe..f116d596` with the card workflow's path list, and no path matches. From `f116d596` to this head, only the note, its manifest and main's report differ, so the gate covers this head's source. The controls index lists 25 controls: 24 name a failed step or assertion, and `next-reads-same` ends on its named timeout, as the request says.\n\nAt this head I ran `apps/views` tests (28 passed), `page-needs-you.test.ts` (7 passed), `page-needs-you.scope.test.ts` (1 passed), the Page's `assets` and `view` tests (19 passed) and the seal test (10 passed). `check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1006 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages` pass, and the worktree is clean. I did not rerun the browser scene or the two timeouts that the note reports, and their cause stays unproved.\n\n**Architecture.** Moving the walk out of `reads.ts` and `repo-in-ai.ts` gives both lists one source of rows and words, which is what the planner asked for. The Page gains one read and one section, and no definition, migration or setting changes.\n\n**Security.** No act, no new authority and no seal moves. The list's rows grant nothing, and the scope still judges each press. The note's bounds entry is accurate: the Page has no request, page or byte counter. The six-lane window and the 20 s deadline bound this read in practice.\n\n**Simplification.** The head removes the duplicate walk. `decidedLine` and the other words sit in `attention.ts` beside the row words, which is the right place.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:427e9ecbc22ec34ee3a6df2095235a68f01252ff","binding":"assigned","head":"c5f142737250b547d7c98b8a40140b6587c72121","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1df716a50aaff24db21af9fc08378502ca373a68\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af914fbf8ccccb78c237d68e1721c2e347016245\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8268feb1f346003803e5146499c73a5eae65ccd5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af914fbf8ccccb78c237d68e1721c2e347016245","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}